{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-111890",
  "enisaUuid": "6d74988c-f9b2-36b5-846f-dea178d15639",
  "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntcp: fix use-after-free in do_tcp_getsockopt(TCP_CC_INFO)\n\ndo_tcp_getsockopt() reads icsk->icsk_ca_ops and dereferences the\nget_info function pointer without rcu_read_lock(). With BPF struct_ops\ncongestion control, ca_ops can point to dynamically allocated memory\nthat is freed concurrently, resulting in a use-after-free when the\nkernel dereferences or calls through the stale pointer.\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in do_tcp_getsockopt+0x2037/0x23e0\n  Read of size 8 at addr ffff888013701258 by task exploit/149\n   do_tcp_getsockopt+0x2037/0x23e0 (net/ipv4/tcp.c:4564)\n   tcp_getsockopt+0x91/0xf0\n   __sys_getsockopt+0xf7/0x170\n\nFix this by wrapping the ca_ops load and get_info call within\nrcu_read_lock()/rcu_read_unlock(), and using READ_ONCE() to load\nthe icsk_ca_ops pointer.",
  "datePublished": "Oct 28, 2026, 10:34:49 AM",
  "dateUpdated": "Oct 30, 2026, 12:42:10 PM",
  "baseScore": 0.0,
  "references": "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c312f17917455eedcea29735fa302ebb93cb9b9\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66b831b427301a9c3e485564009d476631413103\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a8b024cbf62b497062c86995737fc303e4cc384e\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8d5fc9e6dc09174d0da6e59678eb8e01a890cbd3\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e057d201640eebb8ed47ec924872c41570a3bd28\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86814e5370068ec2bf0caa6e6d55c3e5bfc6c324\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39aa489e85752f9de214edb0f85e4d578e57af29\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/385e474086c2e7e29e2dded690be40dc273e20ee\n",
